WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:01.054
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.054 --> 00:00:01.887
- [Narrator] This little white tablet

00:00:01.887 --> 00:00:03.830
is more explosive than dynamite.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:06.037
Sermons have been preached on it.

00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:07.583
Men and women have argued over it.

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.883
- I can't believe that she's
ours and she's in our lives.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.733
- [Woman] Fantasy is
fantasy and it turns us on.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.030
It can remain in your head or sometimes

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.880
you can actually make them a reality.

00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:24.312
- It's a cautious thing, I
want to pick my fertility.

00:00:31.013 --> 00:00:32.987
- [Janelle] In France, they
call the moment of attraction

00:00:32.987 --> 00:00:35.437
(speaks in foreign language)
or a lightning bolt.

00:00:37.221 --> 00:00:40.365
In Arabic, (speaks in
foreign language), a wind.

00:00:40.365 --> 00:00:43.170
In China, (speaks in foreign
language), a fated forest.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:46.280
And in Japan, they say
(speaks in foreign language)

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.030
the feeling when you meet someone

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.740
that you're bound to fall in love.

00:00:50.815 --> 00:00:53.631
- How do I know if I'm
attracted to someone?

00:00:53.631 --> 00:00:57.710
- It's just kind of this like, magnetic,

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.900
but it's just kind of like,

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.000
I just feel drawn to that person.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.180
- When you're attracted to somebody,

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:05.750
you shouldn't really be able to explain it

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.752
beyond just like, I'm
attracted to them, right.

00:01:08.752 --> 00:01:10.960
It should just be visceral
and you should know it.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.436
- [Janelle] We're not sure why this shape

00:01:13.436 --> 00:01:15.280
became the universal symbol of love

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:17.250
but one leading theory is that it came

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.160
from the silphium pod so valuable

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.450
across the ancient Mediterranean.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.820
It was printed on the currency
of the only place they grew,

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.553
the Greek colony, Cyrene.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:30.640
It was exported around
the region for all kinds

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.200
of medical uses and one in particular.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.840
Soranus of Ephesus, the
foremost gynecologist

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.090
of his time advised women
to drink silphium juice

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:43.280
once a month, since it not
only prevents conception

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:46.113
but also destroys any already existing.

00:01:48.057 --> 00:01:49.656
Which means our modern heart shape

00:01:49.656 --> 00:01:52.356
may derive from an ancient
kind of morning after pill.

00:01:54.731 --> 00:01:56.290
- The top of the cervix
actually has a lot of muscle

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:59.540
that does contract so that's
what lead us start to think

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.410
okay, well maybe this is the sphincter.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.560
And so that actually
completely changes the map

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.300
that we're working with to understand

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.180
what goes on in pregnancy

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.310
because in women who deliver early

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.880
that cervix starts to open prematurely

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.040
and it might actually be a sphincter

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.673
that's relaxing too soon.

00:02:16.203 --> 00:02:17.440
- [Janelle] But why that
happens in one patient

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.970
over another, we don't fully understand.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.330
- Mechanics obviously play
a really important role

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.370
in pregnancy.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.560
I do need an engineer
to help me understand

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.370
how strong is the tissue.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.400
- We can run what ifs scenarios.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.550
So what if the patient has a short cervix?

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:36.250
Will her cervix open if the baby kicks

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.050
or if there's a small contraction?

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:41.476
Can that cervix mechanical withstand

00:02:41.476 --> 00:02:43.230
the lows of pregnancy?

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:46.360
- We should know those answers,
I mean, we're curing cancer,

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:49.180
we should be able to understand
pregnancy a lot better.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.930
- [Janelle] Male germ cells in the testes

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:54.030
don't start producing sperm until puberty.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:57.560
A germ cell divides into
two identical copies.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.090
One keeps dividing and
those cells become sperm

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:04.300
but the other stays a germ
cell so they don't run out

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.623
and a man can produce
new sperm until old age.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.650
But in a female fetus, those
germ cells in the ovaries

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.253
start turning into
immature eggs right away.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.410
A 20 week old fetus has
roughly seven million of them

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.580
but they quickly start wasting away.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.740
A female newborn is left
with about two million

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:25.990
and by the time the first one

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.640
makes it's day view in puberty,

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.850
she's down to three or
four hundred thousand.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.290
And then every month one egg is released

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.150
and a thousand or so more die off.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.300
And that's why most women
have a much harder time

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.850
getting pregnant after
40 and are pretty much

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:43.402
out of eggs by the time they're 50.

00:03:43.402 --> 00:03:46.220
Doulas aren't doctors or midwives,

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.280
they're trained birth coaches.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.080
They're to support the laboring woman

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.980
and help make sure her
wishes are being respected

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.273
by the medical provider.

00:03:55.119 --> 00:03:56.423
(moaning)

00:03:56.423 --> 00:03:59.380
- You're so strong, look at you.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.880
- [Janelle] A number of
studies have confirmed

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.226
the presence of a doula reduces
the need of interventions,

00:04:04.226 --> 00:04:08.270
finding a 51% decrease in C-sections.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.420
- I think it's partly just that it's nice

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:14.066
to have somebody in the room
to say, yeah, this is normal,

00:04:14.066 --> 00:04:17.800
this is okay, everything is going fine.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.223
I think that that part
of labor is quite scary.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.154
(moaning)

00:04:25.154 --> 00:04:26.740
- We're almost there, sweetheart.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:27.793
We are almost there.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:31.370
- [Janelle] And the natural
childbirth movements

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.530
underlying message continues to resonate

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:37.920
around the world that women
should make their own choices

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.120
based on what's best for them.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:43.690
On TV, low sperm count is
often treated as a joke,

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:46.110
like the risks posed by hot tubs.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.350
- Mr. Truman?
- Yes.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.212
- We need to talk about your sperm.

00:04:49.212 --> 00:04:52.080
- (gasps) I knew it, it's
the jacuzzi at the gym,

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.576
he boiled them didn't he?

00:04:53.576 --> 00:04:54.409
(audience laughs)

00:04:54.409 --> 00:04:55.520
- [Janelle] And too tight underwear.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.430
- Look, you gotta help me I
have to get off jockey shorts.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.320
- You have a low sperm count?

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.610
- Very low.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.400
- [Janelle] And excessive masturbation.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.910
- Sample hardly had any swimmers.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.850
- That's probably from
excessive masturbation,

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:10.819
the guy's been outpacing his
ability to produce sperm.

00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:14.320
- [Janelle] Daily ejaculation
has no major negative effect

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:17.990
on semen parameters, as
in sperm count or quality.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:21.400
As for tight underwear, one study found,

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.750
semen parameters gradually decrease

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.930
while the subjects were
in tight conditions

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.530
but they gradually increased

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:31.600
while they were in loose conditions.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.740
And the wet heat of hot tubs

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:36.740
can also temporarily lower sperm count,

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:40.130
but only DJ Khaled level of
jacuzzi time could do that.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:43.750
For the record, DJ Khaled's
sperm seems totally fine.

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.060
See, he's got a son.

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.360
Scientists figured out how

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.800
to hack the male reproduction
system decades ago.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:54.100
And large trials in the
1970's showed some promise,

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.270
the perfection of male birth control

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.780
seemed right around
the corner for decades.

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:00.980
- The Chinese have developed what they say

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.390
is a safe and effective
birth control pill for men.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:06.190
- Medical researchers reported today

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:08.360
they have found the chemical
that may hold the key

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.080
to a male birth control pill.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.130
- International research
teams are working on

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:13.160
an injectable--

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.100
- Birth control pill form.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.220
- Men are taking part in the first trials

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.240
of a new form of birth control.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.073
- For men.

00:06:19.073 --> 00:06:19.906
- Birth control for men.

00:06:19.906 --> 00:06:20.739
- Male birth control.

00:06:20.739 --> 00:06:21.760
- Male birth control pill.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.240
- Male birth control
may be one step closer

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.100
to becoming a reality.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.020
- [Janelle] But it never arrived.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.090
Since trials were often cut short

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.370
because men faced too many side affects,

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.370
side affects that might sound familiar

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:38.640
like mood swings, acne
and a loss of libido.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:41.870
When approving the drug,
the FDA weighs it's risks

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.860
against the risks of not taking that drug

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.030
and men unlike women don't
personally face the risks

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:52.260
that come with pregnancy and
child birth, like blood clots.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.300
Male birth control just
has to meet a higher bar.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:58.220
And drug companies aren't
sure male birth control

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:00.520
has a market to make that worth it.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.360
- I'll be open to it, does
that make me less of a man,

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.680
I don't know but I'm open
to anything, honestly.

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.220
- If guys had the option
to take that level

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:12.856
of responsibility like leveling
up from just using a condom,

00:07:12.856 --> 00:07:14.870
I think that make it
a fairer conversation.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.563
It takes two people to
accidentally get pregnant.

